{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>He shall not anoint.</b> Rabbi Marinus said that ייסך is like יוסך, and like it is ויישם בארון (Genesis 50:26), like ויושם. The meaning: for it was the custom of Israel to anoint with oil, males as well as females, for thus it is written ושמן לא תסוך (Deuteronomy 28:40). And to anoint from this oil is forbidden to a priest, also to others, for the anointing oil is poured upon the head of the anointed one." "<b>And in its proportion.</b> The spices mentioned above, and in their weight."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The defected spellings ייסך/יוסך refer to forms with and without vav respectively; Ibn Ezra argues the root has an alef that drops orthographically."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:29.137309735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}